  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Cream butter, sugar and egg. Add dry ingredients alternating with milk. Coat cranberries with a bit of flour before adding to mixture. Bake in a 9 x 9 cake pan at 370 degrees for 40 minutes.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine sauce ingredients and cook over low heat, stirring constantly, until thick.  Pour over cake and serve while still warm.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [],
  "nutrition": null,
  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "I doubled the ingredients and baked it in a 9 x 13 pan. The cake didn’t rise quite as high as I expected, perhaps due to the weight of the cranberries or the size of the pan, but no one complained!  When I doubled the sauce, I had to reduce the amount of half and half so that it would thicken, then it tasted a little too sweet. So if you double the sauce, reduce the cream and sugar by ¼ cup. You can always add more cream if it gets too thick. Enjoy!"
    }
  ],
